<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  modern34 — targetSdk 34, scoped storage.

  Reaches the same OEM recordings through MediaStore plus All-files access
  instead of raw paths. Better on every axis except the one S1 measured, which
  is why both flavours ship and M0 decides.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!-- UC-14: the OEM recordings folder is not a media collection this app
         owns, and under scoped storage nothing narrower reaches it. This is the
         single most alarming screen in the whole install (R17) and it is the
         price of the preferred capture route on a modern target. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE" />

    <!-- UC-14: the MediaStore audio query that locates the recording, on the
         API 33+ split of READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_MEDIA_AUDIO" />

    <!--
      ⚠️ DO NOT ADD `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_PHONE_CALL` OR THE `phoneCall`
      FOREGROUND-SERVICE TYPE HERE. SPEC §7.2 lists them; they are wrong, and
      this comment exists so nobody adds them back from the SPEC.

      On API 34 the `phoneCall` type requires the app to be the default dialer,
      to hold MANAGE_OWN_CALLS, or to be a device owner. BonviCall is none of
      the three and CANNOT BECOME ANY OF THEM: it observes calls rather than
      managing them, and the handsets are the employees' own, so device-owner
      provisioning is out of scope (REQUIREMENTS.md §5.7). Starting a foreground
      service of a type the app does not qualify for throws SecurityException —
      so this is not an M0 measurement, it is a crash on every API 34 device.

      This flavour therefore runs on `microphone|dataSync`, which is what
      src/main/AndroidManifest.xml already declares. Nothing is overridden here.
      S1-RECORDING.md's finding that "targetSdk 29+ restricts the phoneCall FGS
      type" is the same fact, arrived at from the other direction.
    -->

</manifest>
